## Full commands and environment (recorded verbatim)

1. Attribution run (profile mode; per-op sync so graphs disabled):
   ```
   cd /mnt/d/CODEX\ WORKSPACE/beellama-escha
   ESCHA_PROFILE=1 GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_GRAPHS=1 \
     ./build-cuda-exp04-stage1/bin/llama-bench \
     -m /mnt/d/CODEX\ WORKSPACE/escha-w2-lowgpu/weights/escha-w2-lowgpu-mono-parity.gguf \
     --prompt-tokens-file /mnt/d/CODEX\ WORKSPACE/escha-w2-lowgpu/evidence/P-ARCH-05/2026-08-29/escha-controlled-server-002/shared-2048.ids \
     -p 2048 -n 0 -ngl 99 -b 2048 -ub 2048 -ctk f16 -ctv f16 -fa on \
     -r 1 -o json -oe json
   ```
   exit=0. stderr: stage1-profile.stderr (800 ESCHA_PROFILE lines).

2. Timed control (graphs on, production gate; graphs are compiled in via
   GGML_CUDA_GRAPHS=ON and active by default for Escha ops unless
   ESCHA_DISABLE_CUDA_GRAPHS is set):
   ```
   ESCHA_ALLOW_CUDA_GRAPHS=1 \
     ./build-cuda-exp04-stage1/bin/llama-bench \
     -m /mnt/d/CODEX\ WORKSPACE/escha-w2-lowgpu/weights/escha-w2-lowgpu-mono-parity.gguf \
     --prompt-tokens-file /mnt/d/CODEX\ WORKSPACE/escha-w2-lowgpu/evidence/P-ARCH-05/2026-08-29/escha-controlled-server-002/shared-2048.ids \
     -p 2048 -n 0 -ngl 99 -b 2048 -ub 2048 -ctk f16 -ctv f16 -fa on \
     -r 3 -o json -oe json
   ```
   exit=0. JSON: stage1-bench.json; stderr: stage1-bench.stderr.

3. Decode guardrail (graphs on):
   ```
   ESCHA_ALLOW_CUDA_GRAPHS=1 \
     ./build-cuda-exp04-stage1/bin/llama-bench \
     -m /mnt/d/CODEX\ WORKSPACE/escha-w2-lowgpu/weights/escha-w2-lowgpu-mono-parity.gguf \
     -p 0 -n 64 -ngl 99 -b 2048 -ub 2048 -ctk f16 -ctv f16 -fa on \
     -r 3 -o json -oe json
   ```
   exit=0. JSON: stage1-decode.json; stderr: stage1-decode.stderr.

Note: ESCHA_ALLOW_CUDA_GRAPHS is the historical ledger name; the current
source uses ESCHA_DISABLE_CUDA_GRAPHS to opt OUT (graphs on by default for
Escha ops). Timed runs therefore had graphs active.

